## Finding 5 — Hardcoded Data (OWASP A02 + A04: Insecure Design) 🟠 Medium

**Current code:**
```js
{ id: 1, name: 'Alice', email: 'alice@example.com' },
{ id: 2, name: 'Bob',   email: 'bob@example.com'   },
```

Hardcoded data sets a dangerous precedent. Real credentials, tokens, or business logic data frequently end up hardcoded when this pattern is normalised early. It also makes the endpoint permanently static and untestable with real data flows.

**Recommendation:**
```js
// users.repository.js  — separate data access from routing
async function findAllUsers() {
  // Database call goes here; return only non-sensitive fields
  return db.query('SELECT id, name FROM users');
}

// app.js
const { findAllUsers } = require('./users.repository');

app.get('/users', requireAuth, async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const users = await findAllUsers();
    res.json(users);
  } catch (err) {
    next(err); // Centralised error handler (see Finding 7)
  }
});
```

