```bash
# .gitignore
.env
.env.*
*.env
```

2. Never store real credentials in any `.env` file that touches a repo — use a secrets manager (AWS Secrets Manager, HashiCorp Vault, Doppler) or CI/CD environment injection.

3. Audit your git history for past commits of these files:
```bash
git log --all --full-history -- '*.env*'
git log --all --full-history -- '.env*'
