| Severity | Finding | OWASP Category |
|----------|---------|----------------|
| 🔴 High | No security headers | A05 – Security Misconfiguration |
| 🔴 High | No authentication on `/users` | A01 – Broken Access Control |
| 🔴 High | No rate limiting | A04 – Insecure Design |
| 🟠 Medium | No input validation / body parsing | A03 – Injection |
| 🟠 Medium | No CORS policy | A05 – Security Misconfiguration |
| 🟠 Medium | Hardcoded data / no safe query pattern | A03 – Injection |
| 🟡 Low | No HTTPS enforcement | A02 – Cryptographic Failures |
| 🟡 Low | No centralized error handling | A05 – Security Misconfiguration |
| 🟡 Low | No logging or audit trail | A09 – Security Logging Failures |

---

## ✅ Recommended Dependency List

```bash
npm install helmet cors express-rate-limit express-validator jsonwebtoken morgan
```

The most critical fixes are **authentication on `/users`**, **helmet for security headers**, and **rate limiting** — those three would address the three High findings and significantly harden the attack surface before any other work is done.

