## Finding 6 — 🟠 HIGH: No CORS Policy (OWASP A05 – Security Misconfiguration)

**File:** `app.js`

No CORS configuration is present. Depending on the deployment context this either:
- Blocks all cross-origin requests (breaking legitimate clients), or
- If a permissive CORS middleware is added ad-hoc later, opens the API to cross-site request abuse

**Fix — Explicit allowlist-based CORS:**
```js
const cors = require('cors');

const allowedOrigins = (process.env.ALLOWED_ORIGINS || '').split(',').filter(Boolean);

app.use(cors({
  origin: (origin, callback) => {
    // Allow non-browser tools (Postman, curl) in development only
    if (!origin && process.env.NODE_ENV === 'development') return callback(null, true);
    if (allowedOrigins.includes(origin)) return callback(null, true);
    callback(new Error(`CORS policy: origin '${origin}' not allowed`));
  },
  methods: ['GET', 'POST', 'PUT', 'DELETE'],
  allowedHeaders: ['Content-Type', 'Authorization'],
  credentials: true,
  maxAge: 86400, // cache preflight for 1 day
}));
```

